From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahnaf Shahriar <ahnaf.shahriar@neuralink.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] STM32G0DMA: Remove valueProviderCallback that clobbers
 channel enable

The EN bit in the channel configuration register (CCR) had a
valueProviderCallback that always returned false. Since Renode's
register framework applies valueProviderCallback by mutating
UnderlyingValue during ReadInner(), any MMIO read of CCR (including
firmware read-modify-write sequences) permanently cleared the stored
EN bit. This caused channelEnable.Value to return false, making
TryTriggerTransfer() reject all peripheral DMA requests.

Remove the valueProviderCallback so the EN flag retains its
firmware-written state. Peripheral-to-memory DMA channels (e.g.
USART RX) now stay enabled and accept GPIO-triggered transfers.

---
 .../Peripherals/DMA/STM32G0DMA.cs             | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/DMA/STM32G0DMA.cs b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/DMA/STM32G0DMA.cs
index 00f7aac79..4e62e2628 100644
--- a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/DMA/STM32G0DMA.cs
+++ b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/DMA/STM32G0DMA.cs
@@ -214,7 +214,7 @@ public Channel(STM32G0DMA parent, int number)
                                 DoTransfer();
                             }
                         },
-                        valueProviderCallback: _ => false, name: "Channel enable (EN)")
+                        name: "Channel enable (EN)")
                     .WithFlag(1, out transferCompleteInterruptEnable, name: "Transfer complete interrupt enable (TCIE)")
                     .WithFlag(2, out halfTransferInterruptEnable, name: "Half transfer interrupt enable (HTIE)")
                     .WithTag("Transfer error interrupt enable (TEIE)", 3, 1)
